<template>
    <SiteShell page="features">
        <div class="page-head">
            <h1>Features</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                One case model behind validation, solving and exchange. Create
                and edit an `.ocfd` case, solve a two-dimensional incompressible
                flow, inspect residuals and forces, and export the field today.
                Three-dimensional flow, compressible flow, buoyancy and external
                import are labelled as unsupported instead of being implied by a
                suffix.
            </p>
            <div class="head-tags">
                <span class="chip chip--available">solver core available</span>
                <span class="chip chip--blocked">no graphical viewport</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Contracts</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid-2">
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Session API</h3>
                    <p>
                        <code>OpenCfd</code> owns create, open, edit, validate,
                        solve, export and save. The CLI, the Node-API addon and the
                        TypeScript SDK call the same Rust session, so they cannot
                        drift into separate solvers.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Atomic writes</h3>
                    <p>
                        Every edit validates and writes the `.ocfd` file through a
                        temporary file plus rename. CSV, VTK and SVG export use the
                        same atomic write path, so a failed solve cannot leave a
                        half-written result.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Stable error codes</h3>
                    <p>
                        Failures carry a code such as <code>mesh/invalid</code>,
                        <code>solver/unstable</code> or
                        <code>capability/not-implemented</code>. The exit code is
                        <code>1</code> for input or IO errors and <code>2</code>
                        for an unsupported capability.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="chip chip--declared">measured</span>
                    <h3>Capability matrix</h3>
                    <p>
                        <code>ocfd capabilities</code> prints the machine-readable
                        matrix from one source of truth. A route is only described
                        as available when its report or export exists in this
                        build.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Feature areas</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--blocked">read the status</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid-3">
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Case document</h3>
                    <p>
                        `.ocfd` cases are UTF-8 JSON with camelCase fields. A
                        minimal file declares only <code>format</code> and
                        <code>version</code>; mesh, fluid, time, boundaries and
                        obstacles have documented defaults.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Mesh and boundaries</h3>
                    <p>
                        A uniform Cartesian mesh carries pressure at cell centres
                        and velocity on staggered faces. Each of the four sides is
                        a wall, inlet or outlet with an explicit velocity.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Solver</h3>
                    <p>
                        Momentum prediction uses first-order upwind convection,
                        central diffusion and explicit Euler. An SOR pressure
                        Poisson solve projects the velocity and removes divergence.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Obstacles and forces</h3>
                    <p>
                        Rectangular and circular obstacles are masked by cell
                        centre. Pressure and viscous shear on solid faces produce
                        per-obstacle <code>Cd</code> and <code>Cl</code> in the
                        report, with <code>fxPressure</code>,
                        <code>fxViscous</code>, <code>fyPressure</code> and
                        <code>fyViscous</code> decomposed separately.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Residuals and convergence</h3>
                    <p>
                        Each step reports the L2 norm of the velocity change. With
                        <code>--tolerance</code> the solve stops at steady state and
                        records the sampled history, pressure residual and
                        iteration count.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                    <h3>Exchange</h3>
                    <p>
                        After a solve, write cell-centred
                        <code>x,y,pressure,u,v,magnitude,temperature</code> CSV,
                        legacy ASCII <code>STRUCTURED_POINTS</code> VTK, or an SVG
                        pressure/temperature field. Derived fields include the
                        pressure coefficient <code>cp</code>, selectable as
                        <code>--field pressureCoefficient</code>.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">executable</span>
                    <h3>Agent skills</h3>
                    <p>
                        The skill document lists the real commands and the real
                        limits. It never presents 3D, compressible flow, buoyancy or
                        external import as executable.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Command surface</h2>
                <span class="chip">today</span>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="matrix">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Surface</th>
                            <th>Today</th>
                            <th>Behaviour</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">CLI</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">available</span></td>
                            <td>Creates, edits, validates, solves and exports cases. Editing commands save the file in place.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">SDK</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">available</span></td>
                            <td><code>new OpenCFD()</code> returns a session; documents expose mesh, fluid, time, boundary, obstacle, scalar, validate, solve and export methods.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">Node-API</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">available</span></td>
                            <td>A thin native wrapper over the same session; the SDK resolves the platform addon from the package name.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">Skills</td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--available">executable</span></td>
                            <td>Records routing rules and the exact commands that work in this build.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Capability honesty</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--declared">measured</span>
            </div>
            <p>
                The capability matrix reports two-dimensional cavity and channel
                cases, obstacles, passive scalar transport, convergence detection,
                `.ocfd` read/write and CSV/VTK/SVG export as supported. It reports
                compressible flow, turbulence, coupled heat transfer,
                three-dimensional flow and external import as
                <code>capability/not-implemented</code>. A request for those
                routes fails; it is not approximated silently.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Current state</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--available">inspectable</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid-2">
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="status-dot status-dot--on"></span>
                    <h3>In place</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Case document and atomic `.ocfd` persistence</li>
                        <li>Mesh, fluid, time, boundary and obstacle editing</li>
                        <li>Passive scalar (temperature) transport</li>
                        <li>Staggered solver with pressure projection</li>
                        <li>Steady-state detection and residual history</li>
                        <li>Obstacle force coefficients</li>
                        <li>CSV, VTK and SVG export</li>
                        <li>CLI and SDK on the same Rust core</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <span class="status-dot status-dot--off"></span>
                    <h3>Not implemented</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Three-dimensional and axisymmetric flow</li>
                        <li>Compressible flow</li>
                        <li>Boussinesq buoyancy and coupled heat transfer</li>
                        <li>Body-fitted, adaptive and moving meshes</li>
